  "id": "ex-18-futur-a2",
  "intro": "Standalone drill set, not tied to any lesson. German rarely needs a separate future tense — Präsens + a time word (Morgen fahre ich nach Berlin) is usually enough and is what native speakers actually say. Futur I (werden + Infinitiv at the end) shows up for predictions, promises, and firm intentions where the \"will happen\" nuance matters: Es wird morgen regnen. Nächstes Jahr werde ich mein Studium beenden. Blocks: A Basistraining → B Vertiefung → C Sprachbausteine → D Wiederholung. Answers in solutions.md.\n",
  "lesson": "EX/18-futur-a2",
  "level": "A2",
  "summary": null,
  "title": "Futur I: werden + Infinitiv — A2",
  "topic": "Futur I und II"
}
